<title>USA: Jacor to swap station for three others.</title>
<headline>Jacor to swap station for three others.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jacor Communications Inc said on Friday it has entered into an agreement to exchange the assets of a radio station in Cincinnati for the assets of three Rochester, N.Y., radio stations owned by American Radio Systems Corp.</p>
<p>Jacor plans to swap its WKRQ-FM for American Radio's WHAM-AM, WHTK-AM and WVOR-FM. In addition, American Radio would assign Jacor an option to purchase WNVE-FM, a Rochester radio station.</p>
<p>Financial details were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The transactions are subject to regulatory approval.</p>
<p>The agreement is part of Jacor's requirement to divest WKRQ-FM as a result of its acquisition of Citicasters Inc.</p>
</text>
